      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_1234161" metaid="metaid_25" name="HIF-alpha translocates from cytosol to nucleus" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">HIF-alpha (HIF1A, EPAS1, HIF3A isoform 1) is translocated into the nucleus (Kallio et al. 1998, Depping et al. 2008, Chachami et al. 2009, Heikkilä et al. 2011). Importin 4 and importin 7 (Chachami et al. 2009) as well as the importin alpha/beta pathway (Depping et al. 2008) appear to be capable of interacting with HIF-alpha. During hypoxia HIF-alpha accumulates in the nucleus where it associates with CBP and p300 (Kallio et al. 1998).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
