      <reaction compartment="compartment_7660" fast="false" id="reaction_1235070" metaid="metaid_28" name="Expression of Erythropoietin (EPO)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The EPO gene is transcribed to yield mRNA and the mRNA is translated to yield protein. Transcription of EPO is enhanced by Hypoxia-inducible factor, which binds to the EPO promoter. The HIF heterodimer binds the promoter of the EPO gene and recruits p300 and CBP to enhance transcription of EPO.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
